mso-border-left-alt:none;border-right:1.0000pt solid windowtext;mso-border-right-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;
border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;border-bottom:1.0000pt solid windowtext;
mso-border-bottom-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;">
                    <p class=MsoNormal><span style="font-family:仿宋;mso-bidi-font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:12.0000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><font face="仿宋"><p>This course guides students to apply recognized ethical standards and morality to their future medical practice and research by teaching the basic concepts, connotations, and fundamental principles and regulatory guidelines to be followed in medical ethics, as well as through case analysis discussions and experience sharing in clinical practice and research processes. By teaching the overview of medical rule of law, the legal system of medical subjects, and the legal system of medical behaviors, students can theoretically understand the general situation of the medical legal system and be aware of the rights and obligations of medical and health workers in their future practical work in terms of content, laying a solid foundation for correctly fulfilling job responsibilities, practicing medicine in accordance with the law, protecting human health, and promoting the development of the health care industry and people's health in the future.</p></font></span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;font-size:10.5000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><o:p></o:p></span></p>
                </td>
            </tr>
